{
  "scope": "Exact CPU signed-digit RNS conversion used by prepared gadget multiplication and staged factor-table transforms. No changes to encrypted rows, approximation defaults, CRT/NTT layouts, moduli, scales or accuracy gates.",
  "primitive_commit": "2629fb0",
  "gadget_commit": "730f21b",
  "staged_tables_and_controls_commit": "8b9fc59",
  "algorithm": "Convert8 signed int64 coefficients at once. Shuffle contiguous loads into even/odd64-bit lanes, take unsigned magnitudes (including2^63), apply widened Montgomery reduction, normalize, remove the inverse-radix factor with R^2, then restore signs canonically. Scalar modulo remains available for controls and non-AVX2 builds.",
  "integer_bounds": "For every selected prime,2^31/3<p<2^30. Signed magnitudes t<=2^63 and the low-word correction m<2^32 imply t+m*p<3*2^62<2^64. REDC(t)<2^31+p<4p<2^32. Subtraction/min folds below2p then p, with no overflow or precision approximation. Multiplying by R^2 and reducing restores t modulo p. Negative zero is normalized to0.",
  "storage": "For staged plaintext scales below63 bits, retain int64 coefficients instead of pair<bool,uint64_t>; this uses8 rather than16 bytes per coefficient on the tested build. Preserve the old unsigned-magnitude path for larger scales. The existing proved coefficient-magnitude check remains. Gadget input digits and prepared key spectra retain their existing representations.",
